     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi there, <br></div><div><br></div><div>I have a fairly large genlight file with geo-referenced data, but I have about 10% missing data. When I try to use the gl.ibd function, I get this error message:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span><span style=\"color:blue\">ibd_all80 &lt;- gl.ibd(ALL_MPB_gl)</span></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in kde2d(Dgeo, Dgen, n = 300) : \r\n  missing or infinite values in the data are not allowed<br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">When</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"> I run a PCA, I usually deal with NA values using the tab method (like this: <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">all_noNAs &lt;- tab(</span></span></span></span></span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span>ALL_MPB_gl</span>, NA.method=&quot;mean&quot;</span></span>). <br><br>Is there a way of dealing with the missing values here? I am fairly confident that I have the spatial coordinates inputted correctly as I modeled them off the ones in the <a href=\"http://bandicoot.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bandicoot.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792459142953000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1vv4NnqHQvA_BfB3VToca1\">bandicoot.gl</a> file.</span></span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br>I also get a similar error when I use the by individual IBD method that is listed in the other dartR post about IBD</span></span>.<br><br></span></span><span><span style=\"color:blue\">mantel(ed,gd)</span></span><br><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in cor(as.vector(xdis), ydis, method = method, use = use) : \r\n  missing observations in cov/cor</span></span></span></span></pre></div></div>"
